# ── cross-repo dev link ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE of the two halves is ignored, and the asymmetry is deliberate.
#
#  · `ru-code-packages` — a SYMLINK to the local packages checkout. Developer-local:
#    every machine points it somewhere different, so it is ignored, and it is the line
#    below.
#  · `.pnpmfile.cjs` — TRACKED, not ignored. It rewrites every `@smart-tools/*`
#    dependency onto that symlink, and every clone needs it, because the SDK and the
#    dev tooling are not published yet. It is INERT without the symlink (`linkActive`
#    is false), so a clone that has no sibling checkout installs from the registry
#    unchanged — which is what CI gets, and what happens the day the SDK publishes.
#
# See the README, "Local development against unpublished packages", for the two steps
# and for switching the link off. The pnpmfile's own header says the same thing.
ru-code-packages

# local dev link to an unpublished SDK checkout (never committed)
.pnpmfile.cjs
.playground
